Frontend is the visible, interactive part of a website or application that users interact with directly in their web browser. It is built using core web technologies like HTML for structure, CSS for styling, and JavaScript for functionality and responsiveness. Ultimately, its main goal is to provide a seamless, accessible, and user-friendly experience by properly presenting data delivered from the backend.
