Backend is the behind-the-scenes part of a website or application that handles data storage, security, and business logic. It consists of a server, a database, and an application that processes requests and delivers the necessary information to the frontend. Built using languages like Python, Java, or Node.js, its main job is to ensure the entire system runs smoothly, securely, and efficiently.
